  {
    "episode_id": 75527,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75527.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 34,
    "turn_text": "Well, of course, we have to back up and do you think that Cory Booker or Tammy Baldwin or Elizabeth Warren have any credibility when they made all kinds of allegations and promises about Obamacare and the number of people that have been hurt and devastated because in Wisconsin alone, you've had a doubling of premiums. Your premiums have gone up by 100% since this law was enacted and they promised us our premiums not only wouldn't go up, but they would actually go down. And we would be able to keep our doctors and we keep our healthcare plans. All of those promises were false. And so now they're coming out again trying to scare the American people when they have zero damn credibility on healthcare. They've lied. They've lied to the American people. And so now we're supposed to believe them. Listen, we understand in rural parts of America and in places like mine, you only have one option for healthcare coverage. and across other rural states and rural counties, they don't have any providers. So Obamacare is imploding. And what we're trying to do is give families more say in the healthcare coverage that they buy. Instead of having mandates and dictates come from Washington, we want to give you a little more say in the healthcare coverage that you buy that fits the risks in your life, which means if you have a more targeted healthcare plan, you can actually reduce your premiums. And we understand in every space of the economy, competition offers lower prices and better service. They don't listen. These are socialist. They don't believe in competition.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
