    "turn_text": "in markets. They believe in government control. And that's at the root of this debate. And you have liberals and progressives who are hell bent on making sure government control every damn aspect of our lives. And this is the great fight of our generation, the enemy. We're fighting this at every corner, but the heart of the fight right now is in health care. And we're fighting to give you control, and Democrats are fighting to give more control to the federal government. And I look at this too. I hope this week, and I'm not sure what Tammy Baldwin is going to do, but Tammy Baldwin, as a supporter of a failed health care plan that has hurt tens of thousands of Wisconsinites. I hope conservatives, actually, instead of Republicans taking the brunt of phone calls and rallies, and we're getting calls for four-town halls, which I do a lot of them. We should be calling Tammy Baldwin out. Where are her town halls? When does she answer to Wisconsin voters to say, you know what? I'm not going to lift a finger to fix failed healthcare that I gave Wisconsin. I'm going to try to wash my hands of it and take a bazooka to Republicans who are trying to do the right thing to make healthcare work for Wisconsin. Where is Tammy Baldwin as part of this solution? Well, he is conservative. Can't just look at Ron Johnson who is going to have to get on board. He's got to get some of the tweaks. And I think he'll get there. But Tammy Baldwin has absolutely failed our state and our country.",
